  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is a Williamson&#39;s ether synthesis reaction. It is a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;reaction. Aryl halides will not undergo nucleophilic substitution reactions readily. Hence, allyl-phenyl ether can be prepared by reaction of allyl halide and phenoxide ion as follows</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/9d81acde-820c-4941-bd2e-fdfcbcf50301-image.png\" style=\"width: 392px; height: 86px;\" /></p>",
